from pathlib import Path
import json,html
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
media=json.loads((H/'media-index.json').read_text());cards=[]
for r in media:
 cards.append('<article><h2>'+html.escape(r['episode'])+'</h2><img src="media/'+r['file']+'"><p>'+str(r['samples'])+' native samples · '+str(r['durationMs']/1000)+' seconds</p></article>')
text='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Krusher Dom · In-game animation review</title><style>body{font:17px system-ui;background:#172127;color:#dce6e8;max-width:1150px;margin:40px auto;padding:20px}p{line-height:1.55;color:#c3d1d5}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:25px}article{background:#243138;padding:18px;border-radius:12px}h2{font-size:17px}img{max-width:100%;image-rendering:pixelated}a{color:#9bd8de}</style><h1>Krusher Dom · In-game motion review</h1><p>Current V11 candidate in the actual game renderer. Sitting and reading use registered authored furniture contacts. Workshop sequences use production entry, work, pickup, carrying and unloading. All 72 carrying/swimming turn trials use production movement and transition clearance.</p><p>These replays align native screenshot crops at the declared foot for close inspection. They reconstruct simulation time from source/position-change captures; they are not full-room real-time videos. Replay loops reset to the start. Water lighting is retained.</p><div class="cards">'''+''.join(cards)+'''</div><p>Source art, timing and normal crew selection are unchanged in this pass. Verification reports distinguish staged contacts, production activity updates and staged locomotion turn trials. Owner visual acceptance and normal roster integration remain separate.</p>'''
(H/'index.html').write_text(text,encoding='utf-8');print('Wrote native replay review')
